## Products

There are many products for different needs, including pads, pants, men's guards and washable products. **Bladder and Bowel UK** has free advice on choosing products.

## Skin care

Change products regularly, wash with water or a gentle cleanser, and use a barrier cream if needed.

## Going out

- plan toilet stops
- carry spare products and a change of clothes
- a **Radar key** opens thousands of locked accessible toilets. See [accessible toilets](/support/leisure/accessible-toilets/)

## Relationships

Incontinence can affect sex and confidence. Empty your bladder first, and talk to your partner. Your GP or physiotherapist can help.

## Support

**Bladder and Bowel UK** runs a free helpline.
